WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.722
Ben looked at his stool in surprise.

2
00:00:04.782 --> 00:00:07.484
It was halfway across the room.

3
00:00:07.584 --> 00:00:12.407
Ben, however, was floating exactly where he'd been.

4
00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:13.248
Mog lay sprawled on the floor.

5
00:00:13.268 --> 00:00:17.170
"He tried to knock me over!"

6
00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:32.349
Ben realized.

7
00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:35.571
"Mog!" cried Mrs.

8
00:00:35.631 --> 00:00:38.253
Hag. "What are you doing?"

9
00:00:38.273 --> 00:00:41.295
The monster got up off the floor.

10
00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:45.098
"I was, um, trying to get my stool back."

11
00:00:46.098 --> 00:00:48.740
He pointed to the stool he had knocked across the room.

12
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.863
"That's not your stool," said Mrs.

13
00:00:52.903 --> 00:00:56.286
Hag. "That's Ben's stool.

14
00:00:56.806 --> 00:00:59.448
Now sit down and behave yourself!"

15
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.801
Mog sat down as Ben got the stool.

16
00:01:04.762 --> 00:01:08.863
When Ben came back, Mog leaned over the table, scowling at him.

17
00:01:08.883 --> 00:01:15.166
"Listen, you pathetic excuse for a monster," Mog whispered.

18
00:01:15.186 --> 00:01:21.148
"Stay away from Winnie, or you'll end up all alone, haunting a ghost town!"

19
00:01:21.168 --> 00:01:24.110
"Oh, Mog," said Winnie.

20
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.991
"He wouldn't be alone in a ghost town.

21
00:01:27.451 --> 00:01:29.212
Those places are filled with ghosts."

22
00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:32.909
She flashed a smile at Ben.

23
00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.632
snarled Mog, still glaring at Ben.

24
00:01:40.652 --> 00:01:44.914
"He's a really nice guy," Winnie whispered to Ben.

25
00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.415
"He's just not showing it today."

26
00:01:49.035 --> 00:01:50.696
Mrs. Hag clapped her hands.

27
00:01:50.716 --> 00:01:53.237
"Let's start cooking!

28
00:01:53.637 --> 00:01:59.820
Mog, get out the soap and scrub brush so you're ready to clean up when we're done."

29
00:02:02.252 --> 00:02:03.732
Ben watched Mog get up.

30
00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:06.553
Ben had stood up to Mog earlier.

31
00:02:07.574 --> 00:02:10.814
But he was new at school, and he couldn't afford to make enemies.

32
00:02:11.935 --> 00:02:14.095
He'd better stay out of Mog's way for now.

33
00:02:15.236 --> 00:02:19.497
Then he stole another quick look at Winnie, hoping she hadn't read his thoughts again.

34
00:02:20.657 --> 00:02:22.498
Maybe he'd better stay out of her way too.

35
00:02:26.639 --> 00:02:30.560
At lunch Gaby told Ben more about the dance that Waldo had mentioned.

36
00:02:32.448 --> 00:02:36.932
And over the next few days, that's all anyone was talking about at Monster Academy.

37
00:02:38.053 --> 00:02:40.635
Who was going with whom to the Monster Mash dance?

38
00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:44.238
Which girl monsters had asked boy monsters?

39
00:02:45.399 --> 00:02:50.443
Why did the girl mummies always spend the evening giggling and running to the restroom to rewrap their

40
00:02:50.463 --> 00:02:56.748
bandages? Ben wanted to go to the dance.

41
00:02:57.824 --> 00:03:01.145
He had already met a bunch of girl monsters at Monster Academy.

42
00:03:01.586 --> 00:03:05.067
But there was only one he really liked—and she was taken.

43
00:03:05.087 --> 00:03:11.930
A few days later during homeroom, Mr.

44
00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.270
Freaky made an announcement.

45
00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.851
"Attention, monsters!"

46
00:03:16.372 --> 00:03:18.412
His voice crackled over the loudspeaker.

47
00:03:18.432 --> 00:03:24.635
"As you know, we've been having some strange problems with our brooms since school started.

48
00:03:25.055 --> 00:03:30.181
We've found brooms everywhere—the restrooms, the gym, the soccer field.

49
00:03:31.101 --> 00:03:33.942
Just yesterday one crashed through my office window!"

50
00:03:33.962 --> 00:03:39.963
"We're not sure who's causing the empty brooms to fly around, but we will find the monster responsible.

51
00:03:40.744 --> 00:03:45.765
In the meantime, because of the danger, we're canceling all extracurricular activities.

52
00:03:46.845 --> 00:03:48.846
That includes the Monster Mash dance."

53
00:03:48.866 --> 00:03:52.727
"What?" "That's not fair!"

54
00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:56.288
Everyone in Ben's homeroom started complaining.

55
00:03:57.452 --> 00:03:59.473
"Furthermore," continued Mr.

56
00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:04.137
Freaky, "all broom-flying classes will be suspended until the broom incidents stop."

57
00:04:04.157 --> 00:04:07.719
"No broom-flying class?"

58
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.941
shrieked a witch sitting next to Winnie.

59
00:04:09.961 --> 00:04:11.802
"That stinks!"

60
00:04:11.822 --> 00:04:13.963
"You're not kidding."

61
00:04:14.484 --> 00:04:16.005
Winnie looked like she might cry.

62
00:04:16.025 --> 00:04:22.469
"My parents promised to get me my own broom as soon as I got my broom- flying license."

63
00:04:24.311 --> 00:04:24.991
She sighed.

64
00:04:26.656 --> 00:04:30.178
"I'll be an ugly old witch before I can fly a broom by myself."

65
00:04:30.198 --> 00:04:37.361
"You could never be an ugly old witch," thought Ben as he gazed over at Winnie.

66
00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:42.383
Winnie suddenly looked up, and her green eyes stared right into his.

67
00:04:43.703 --> 00:04:44.924
Ben looked away quickly.

68
00:04:44.944 --> 00:04:49.166
The bell rang, and all the students headed off to class.

69
00:04:50.186 --> 00:04:54.628
As Ben drifted down the hallway, he thought about the sad look on Winnie's face again.

70
00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.140
Poor Winnie.

71
00:04:56.461 --> 00:04:57.961
She'd looked so disappointed.

72
00:04:59.042 --> 00:05:01.323
Suddenly Ben got a brilliant idea.

73
00:05:01.343 --> 00:05:04.545
"I'll figure out who's crashing the brooms!"

74
00:05:04.925 --> 00:05:05.445
he thought.

75
00:05:05.465 --> 00:05:10.348
"Then Winnie can go back to broom-flying class and get her own broom."

76
00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:19.233
He was new at Monster Academy, but he could find the mysterious broom- flier and help Winnie.

77
00:05:20.374 --> 00:05:21.294
He knew he could.

78
00:05:24.116 --> 00:05:27.450
Later Ben heard a voice behind him in the cafeteria.

79
00:05:28.571 --> 00:05:29.311
It was Gaby.

80
00:05:29.732 --> 00:05:30.912
He turned to look up at her.

81
00:05:30.933 --> 00:05:32.674
"Guess what?"

82
00:05:33.134 --> 00:05:34.695
she cried, jumping up and down.

83
00:05:35.756 --> 00:05:37.737
The entire cafeteria shook.

84
00:05:38.898 --> 00:05:40.399
"Hey, quit jumping!"

85
00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.841
complained a goblin at the next table.

86
00:05:42.861 --> 00:05:45.603
"You spilled my toad juice!"

87
00:05:47.304 --> 00:05:47.785
"What is it?

88
00:05:47.885 --> 00:05:48.345
Tell me!"

89
00:05:48.926 --> 00:05:49.466
said Ben.

90
00:05:50.487 --> 00:05:51.788
Gaby stopped jumping.

91
00:05:52.864 --> 00:05:56.085
"Waldo Wizz asked me to go see a movie on Friday night!"

92
00:05:56.645 --> 00:05:57.165
she said.

93
00:05:57.185 --> 00:05:59.626
"That's fantastic!"

94
00:06:00.046 --> 00:06:00.606
said Ben.

95
00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:04.327
"Waldo is so nice," Gaby gushed.

96
00:06:05.328 --> 00:06:06.228
"He's cute too.

97
00:06:06.588 --> 00:06:08.369
Have I told you about how great he is at magic?"

98
00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:11.890
"Yes." Ben rolled his eyes.

99
00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:19.292
Gaby had told him about Waldo Wizz's magic skills—along with his bright blue eyes—many, many times.

100
00:06:20.364 --> 00:06:24.227
Ben was about to remind Gaby of this when another idea came to him.

101
00:06:25.388 --> 00:06:28.871
Waldo was supposed to be some kind of genius at magic.

102
00:06:30.032 --> 00:06:33.575
Maybe he could help find the monster who was crashing all the brooms.
